{
  "name": "Trigger Debug Detective",
  "version": "2.0.0",
  "description": "Manually trigger the Debug Detective to diagnose a failed automation test run. Analyzes HTML reports, traces test flow, and produces a structured DEBUG_REPORT file.",
  "when": {
    "type": "userTriggered"
  },
  "then": {
    "type": "askAgent",
    "prompt": "You are acting as the QA-Debug-Detective-Agent.\n\nAsk the user:\n1. **Which test class or method failed?** (e.g., 'PayPerItemTest' or 'testPayPerItemWithCashDrawer')\n2. **Which ticket folder?** (e.g., '2026/Q2/Version 229/POS-10501 - ...' or 'field-triage/active/POS-10501')\n\nOnce they provide the info:\n\n1. **RECALL**: Read .kiro/memory/lessons_learned.md and .kiro/memory/pattern_registry.md for known failure patterns.\n\n2. **EVIDENCE COLLECTION**: Search for the HTML execution report in `POS_Automation_UI/pos/target/` folder. Find the most recent report file. Extract: which test methods passed/failed, exact failure step, exception stack traces, last successful log entry before failure.\n\n3. **TRACE**: Walk through the test flow step-by-step. Read the full implementation of every method referenced. Cross-reference with the HTML report.\n\n4. **ANALYZE**: Classify each issue by category (TIMING, REGEX, NULL_SAFETY, DATA_FORMAT, ELEMENT_VISIBILITY, FLOW_LOGIC, LOCATOR) and severity.\n\n5. **OUTPUT**: Write the structured DEBUG_REPORT to the ticket folder as `DEBUG_REPORT.md`. If DEBUG_REPORT.md already exists, MUST overwrite it (not create a second file). Include: Evidence Summary, Findings (severity, category, file, lines, description, evidence, fix, confidence), and Recommended Fix Order.\n\n6. **LEARN**: If new patterns discovered, append to .kiro/memory/pattern_registry.md.\n\nDo NOT apply fixes — only produce the report file. Stop after saving."
  }
}
